Fix crop provider fallback loop overwriting a found crop with NULL.

getCropFromImageStyleId()/findCropForUri() guess the crop type from each
non-"image" effect's provider and loop over every effect, reassigning $crop
on each iteration. When a style stacks a focal point / crop effect together
with another provider's effect that has no matching crop type (e.g.
image_style_quality, as generated by normalized_image_styles), the later
iteration's findCrop() returns NULL and clobbers the crop found earlier.

crop_file_url_alter() then sees no crop and skips the ?h= cache-busting
hash, so focal point changes never invalidate browser/CDN caches.

Stop at the first provider that resolves to a crop.

Applies on top of merge_requests/31.diff.

--- a/src/Entity/Crop.php
+++ b/src/Entity/Crop.php
@@ -210,7 +210,12 @@
         if ($provider === 'image') {
           continue;
         }
-        $crop = self::findCrop($uri, $provider);
+        // Stop at the first provider that resolves to a crop; a later effect
+        // whose provider has no matching crop type (e.g. image_style_quality)
+        // would otherwise overwrite the match with NULL and drop the ?h= hash.
+        if ($crop = self::findCrop($uri, $provider)) {
+          break;
+        }
       }
     }

